{"output":"I'll start by discovering the tools on the tickets and inventory MCP servers.\n\nRate limit hit on 1113. I'll fetch the remaining tickets in smaller batches.\n\nNow per-warehouse stock and existing adjustments.\n\nShipments are done. Now I'll add the comments and set the statuses.\n\nI processed all 25 open `warranty` claims in ticket id order and wrote `/app/STATUS.json` with status `success`. Every tool call I made to ship, comment or set a status succeeded. I did not re-query the tickets or stock afterwards to confirm the final state.\n\n- **Shipped by me (14):** 1107, 1108, 1113, 1114, 1117, 1120, 1122, 1123, 1124, 1126, 1127, 1133, 1134 and 1135, as adjustments `adj-107` to `adj-120`. Each is `resolved`.\n  - 1127 got the successor `PT-1219`, because `PT-1203` is discontinued.\n  - 1133 shipped from north, because west had run out after 1107.\n- **Shipped before me:** 1125 was answered with the existing `adj-102` and is `resolved`. I shipped nothing for it.\n- **Not covered (8), all `closed`:**\n  - 1106, 1110, 1115, 1116 and 1118: warranty expired. 1118 was created one day after its warranty ended, and 1120 was created on the last covered day.\n  - 1121 and 1128: product line excluded.\n  - 1132: serial already replaced. Ticket 1103 had the same serial and its replacement `adj-24` is already shipped.\n- **Backordered:** 1130 is `pending`. It needs 2 units of `PT-1209`, and no warehouse holds 2 (east has 1, west has 1, north has 0). I did not split the shipment.\n- **Duplicate:** 1131 is marked `duplicate` of #1108, which has the same serial.\n\nI added exactly one comment to each claim. Nothing else was changed in the ticket or stock systems.","final_output":"I processed all 25 open warranty claims in ticket id order and wrote /app/STATUS.json with status success. Every tool call I made to ship, comment or set a status succeeded. I did not re-query the tickets or stock afterwards to confirm the final state.\n\n- Shipped by me (14): 1107, 1108, 1113,